{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Sons of</b> — Rabbi Moshe ha-Kohen, of blessed memory, said: This psalm is as written above, and he spoke with the sons of the notable man because of their arrogance when they were young — \"How long will you turn my glory into shame, [loving] emptiness and seeking lies?\" And this shall not stand nor arise nor come to pass — that which you seek is falsehood. According to Rabbi Moshe's opinion, he speaks about the supporters of Absalom."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:14.554365066Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}